LOCATION:WILLIAM J. GODFREY GRADUATE AND EXECUTIVE EDUCATION CENTER
GEO:39.172447;-86.519399
SUMMARY:Kelley Teaching Seminar-Analog Teaching in the Age of AI & Device
  Distraction
DESCRIPTION:The prevalence of electronic devices and artificial intellige
 nce has unquestionably complicated the learning environment in today's co
 llege classroom. While instructors strive to communicate concepts\, expla
 in multiple-step processes\, and invite students to participate in the co
 -creation of knowledge or practice demanding skills\, students unfortunat
 ely often attend first to their devices or ask A.I. to complete their wor
 k.  In this Kelley Teaching Seminar\, we will explore strategies for limi
 ting device distraction and avoiding AI use while considering old-fashion
 ed\, low- or no-tech teaching strategies aimed at helping students master
  skills and internalize the core knowledge they will need for success in 
 the business world and in life.  The seminar will include short presentat
 ions\, ample discussion among colleagues\, and demonstrations to illustra
 te some of the possibilities. I hope you can join us!
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  The prevalence of electronic devices an
 d artificial intelligence has unquestionably complicated the learning env
 ironment in today's college classroom. While instructors strive to commun
 icate concepts\, explain multiple-step processes\, and invite students to
  participate in the co-creation of knowledge or practice demanding skills
 \, students unfortunately often attend first to their devices or ask A.I.
  to complete their work.</p><p>  In this Kelley Teaching Seminar\, we wil
 l explore strategies for limiting device distraction and avoiding AI use 
 while considering old-fashioned\, low- or no-tech teaching strategies aim
 ed at helping students master skills and internalize the core knowledge t
 hey will need for success in the business world and in life.</p><p>  The 
 seminar will include short presentations\, ample discussion among colleag
 ues\, and demonstrations to illustrate some of the possibilities. I hope 
 you can join us!</p>
UID:20261016T130000Z-2430783@events.iu.edu
