 lass="citation-146">Direct Access to a Top Senior Executive:</span><span 
 class="citation-146">Work shoulder-to-shoulder with a veteran who managed
  over</span><span class="citation-146">$4 Billion</span><span class="cita
 tion-146">in international humanitarian aid and led UN refugee delegation
 s</span>.  </li><li id="p-rc_668c47d0e5884af8-106" data-path-to-node="18\
 ,3\,1"><span class="citation-145">Open to ALL staff\, students\, and facu
 lty\, and general public:</span><span class="citation-145">Whether you're
  in HLS\, O'Neill\, Cybersecurity\, Data Science\, or Public Policy—und
 ergrad or grad—these skills transfer directly to tech\, government\, in
 telligence\, and international NGO careers</span>.  </li></ul><h4 data-pa
 th-to-node="20">  Meet the Expert <span class="citation-144">Paula Reed L
 ynch</span><span class="citation-144">spent nearly five decades on the fr
 ont lines of U.S. foreign policy and international relief</span>. <span c
 lass="citation-143">Serving 14 years in the</span><span class="citation-1
 43">Senior Executive Service</span><span class="citation-143">within the 
 Department of State's Bureau of Population\, Refugees\, and Migration (PR
 M)\, Paula oversaw budgets exceeding</span><span class="citation-143">$4 
 billion</span><span class="citation-143">for global disaster and refugee 
 assistance</span>.</h4><ul data-path-to-node="23"><li><p data-path-to-nod
 e="23\,0\,0">      The Highlights:    </p><ul data-path-to-node="23"><li>
